339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The implementation of the AIR and HEALTH Index has posed a challenge for effective communication in the specific case of ozone, as it contemplates the simultaneous use of two indicators of air quality. One to communicate the state of air quality and the associated health risks from exposure to 1-hour average concentrations, and the other to communicate the state of air quality and the associated health risks from exposure to 8-hour average concentrations. This situation frequently leads to the need to communicate to the population, for a single hour, that the air quality condition may be poor, very poor, or extremely poor for one indicator, while for the other, the condition may reflect good or acceptable air quality. This creates confusion among the public about making the best decisions to reduce their exposure to high concentrations of this pollutant. For this reason, only the one-hour index will be applied.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
